<p>Three new <strong>heavy-pigment stain finishes on White Oak</strong> just landed: <strong>Warm Stone</strong>, <strong>Evening Tide</strong>, and <strong>Deep Water</strong>. From across the room they read like painted cabinetry — opaque, modern, color-confident. Up close, the white oak grain telegraphs through the pigment. It's the painted-cabinet look without losing the wood.</p>

